DESCRIPTION:
CIEnP offers a comprehensive package of assays to evaluate cosmetic ingredients for their in vitro efficacy and  safety.  Relatively simple one-cell type monolayer based test methods present a good and cost-efficient starting point. Most cosmetic formulation ingredients will come in contact with skin keratinocytes, melanocytes and possibly fibroblasts; therefore all cell types have been established as common in vitro test systems *. 


## Skin Absorption: 
Skin absorption tests aims to understand the percutaneous absorption following topical exposure of your individual ingredients / chemicals or finished products using our skin absorption assay. CIEnP skin absorption test is performed using human skin. Synthetic membranes can also be employed in Franz cell drug diffusion studies. CIEnP skin absorption test can assess a range of non-radiolabelled test articles, including liquids, solids, semi-solids, pastes, gels, and creams. 

## Toxicity: 
Cytotoxicity tests assess the skin irritation potential on cultured human or mammalian cell lines. Cytotoxicity is the first test to provide reliable insight into the safety of cosmetics and chemicals. Toxic effects on the cellular level could be identified by different viability tests including:  
* Neutral Red Uptake (NRU)
* MTT Assay
* Anexin and 7AAD


## Efficacy in vitro testing on cosmetics and ingredients for supporting for marketing claims:

### Anti-aging:
   - Antioxidant activity (DPPH);
   - Measurement of intracellular reactive oxygen species (ROS);
   - Measurement of glutathione levels; 
   - Lipid peroxidation assay;
   - Apoptosis;
   - Cell proliferation assay;
   - Cell Cycle regulation;
   - Evaluation of extracellular matrix proteins and metalloproteinases;
   - DNA protection;

### Moisturization:
   - Determination of acid hyaluronic;
   - Aquaporin production;

### Vitalizing effect:
  - Cell proliferation assay; 
  - Cell migration assay;
  - Acid hyaluronic and other matrix protein measurement;
  - ATP determination; 
  - Metabolic activity measurement; 

### Calming effect:
  - Proinflammatory cytokine production/release (IL-1β, IL-6, IL-8, TNF-α);
  - PGE-2 determination;

### Skin repair:
  - Expression and activity of Matrix metalloproteinases; 
  - Angiogenesis assay;
  - Wound Healing assessment (scratch test on fibroblasts or keratinocytes); 
  - Cell migration and proliferation assay;

### Antioxidant effect:
* Measurement of intracellular reactive oxygen species (ROS);
* Measurement of glutathione levels; 
* Lipid peroxidation assay;
* Cell proliferation assay;
* Cell Cycle regulation;
* Evaluation of extracellular matrix proteins and metalloproteinases;

### Firmness: 
  - Quantification of skin collagen;
  - Quantification of skin elastin; 
  - Quantification of skin fibronectin;
  - Evaluation of matrix metalloproteinases;
  - Cell proliferation assay;

### Skin pigmentation:
* TRP-1, TRP-2, tyrosinase, MC1R and MITF mRNA cell expression;
* Tyrosinase activity;
* Melanin content

## Techniques:
	Western blot;
        Real time PCR;
        Colorimetric assays;
        Enzyme assays;
        Immunohistochemistry;
        Immunocytochemistry;
        Immunofluorescence;
        Flow cytometry;

